/T (Riley values uninterrupted focus and intentionally seeks distance from social interaction in order to think and reflect. Advanced climbers may prioritize autonomy before seeking feedback. Choosing when and how to receive advice is especially important at higher skill levels. Not all climbers benefit from the same type of feedback. At an advanced level, growth often comes from reflection and self-guided problem solving rather than direct instruction. Route setters are already aware that not all problems work for every body type or skill level.)
